  "body": "## What changed\n\nThe mill column law (d) stood down for every lateral rapid at or above the clearance plane. A clearance plane set inside the stock sent the traverse through uncut stock and the program posted with no warning (#2121).\n\n**Layer 1 - the law (`crates/sim/src/verify`)**\n\n- `rapids.rs`: the clearance gate is gone. Every lateral rapid under the stock top is marched against the column, whatever plane it rides.\n- Two re-reads for the convictions this adds (a lateral rapid at or above the plane). Each only removes a conviction; neither touches a rapid under the plane, so every pre-#2121 conviction keeps its own rules.\n  - `traverse_solids.rs`, `acquit_traverses_by_solids`: the whole tool stack against the stock and part solids under the strip the rapid sweeps. Each facet is clipped to that strip, so a slope is read where the tool is, not at its far vertex. Closed shells only; fails closed.\n  - `prior_traverse.rs`, `acquit_traverses_by_prior`: the stock grid the program ahead left, under the swept capsule, plus the part's own facets (a part reaching out of its stock is never air because the grid is silent about it).\n- `types.rs`: the sentence is now `rapid move N travels through stock (below the clearance plane, or at it below the stock top)`. The variant `RapidInStock` and its file-format name are unchanged.\n\n**Layer 2 - the operation layer (`crates/app`)**\n\n- `operation/clearance_stock.rs` (new): generate's wiring of both re-reads (unposed and 3+2 branches), the path note `Clearance in stock: rapid move N travels through stock at Z ... - the clearance plane Z ... is inside the stock (top Z ...)`, and `operation::clearance_in_stock_advice`.\n- `mcp/edit.rs`: `add_operation` and `edit_operation` answer with that advice as `warning`.\n- Troubleshooting page and the UI fold's test literal follow the new sentence.\n\n## Validate early: a word, not a refusal\n\nI built the creation-time refusal first and dropped it. The door cannot see where the rapids will run (a profile beside the block never crosses it), so it would refuse legal programs, and it refused four standing fixtures at creation (`operations.rs`, `opframe_picks.rs`, `posted_gates`, `turning.rs`). The plane is named at creation instead (upright mill or vertical hole kind, flat-topped stock, nothing ahead in the program), and the law holds the post. Record: `docs/decisions/2121-rapid-at-clearance-in-stock.md`. The app does not show the word yet: #2131.\n\n## Operation families\n\n| Family | Rapid law | Had the gate? | Now |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 2D mill (Face, Contour, Pocket, Adaptive2D, Offset2D, Slot, Trochoidal Slot, Trace, Engrave, Chamfer2D, Circular) | column law (d) | yes | fixed |\n| 3D mill (Pocket3D, Finish3D, Deburr) | column law (d) | yes | fixed |\n| Drilling (Drill, Bore, Thread; vertical) | column law (d) | yes, for links | fixed |\n| Multi-axis upright rapids (Contour5D, Parallel5D, Swarf, Flow5D, MultiAxisRough, MultiAxisContour) | column law (d), posed re-read for leaning rapids | yes | fixed |\n| 3+2 tilted planes of the kinds above | column law (d) in the plane's frame | yes | fixed, with the solids re-read |\n| Turning | meridian law (`turning_rapids.rs`) | no | unchanged |\n| Rotary (RotaryContour, RotaryParallel, RotaryOffset) | `rotary_hits` | no | unchanged |\n| Cross drilling | `rapids_radial.rs` | no | unchanged |\n\n## How tested\n\nNew pins:\n\n- `crates/app/tests/clearance_in_stock.rs` (8): the issue's Contour repro and a Slot are convicted on the traverse at the plane, carry the note, and `post_setup_unwritten` / `post_setup` refuse and write nothing; the same plane after a Face to Z 5 is clean and posts; a Face to Z 9 does not excuse it; a plane at the stock top is clean; the advice speaks on raw flat stock and stands down behind an earlier op, on a tilted plane and on a stepped stock (where the law still convicts); the MCP tools answer with `warning`.\n- `sim` unit tests: `verify::prior_traverse` (7), `verify::traverse_solids` (6). `app` unit tests: `operation::clearance_stock` (3).\n\nRed before: with the gate restored (mutation M1) the Contour, Slot, shallow-Face, stepped-stock and first-op pins fail.\n\nMutation checks, each killed by at least one pin: gate restored; prior always clears; prior re-read off; part guard off; advice off; advice ignores the program ahead; prior re-read also under the plane; advice treats every stock as flat; solids re-read off (kills `stock_source_holes::framed_stock_chamfer_live_refusal_keeps_hint_without_local_move_number`); solids re-read never convicts; solids re-read also under the plane; one clip side skipped; MCP warning off; advice on a tilted plane.\n\nRuns on the final head:\n\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-sim -p camcraft-motion -p camcraft-app --no-fail-fast`: 635 test binaries, all pass (debug, default lanes).\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-sim -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: green, 4 steps, 0 failed, 11.1 min (sim 38 s, motion 4 s, app 551 s, ui 72 s).\n\n## Goldens and existing tests\n\nNo golden file changed. One existing test changed: `operations.rs::an_entry_edit_marks_the_slot_stale_and_the_orbit_proves_itself` asserted exactly one path note. Its fixture is itself unsafe (Slot top Z 0, clearance Z 5 inside a 0..20 block), so it now carries the new `Clearance in stock:` note beside #104's; the two assertions read \"exactly these two height notes\". The #96/#1066/#1091/#1095 pins are unchanged and pass.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The `--ignored` release heavy lanes and the pixel snapshots.\n- No cut on a machine; no hand-test in the app.\n- Windows and Linux (run on macOS only).\n- A path cached before this fix keeps its cached warnings until it is regenerated (the op stamp salt was not bumped).\n- A part or stock mesh that is not one closed shell gets no solids re-read: its traverse convictions stand (fail closed), which can refuse a legal low-clearance program on such a mesh.\n\n## Overlap\n\nThe #1559 worker's branch (`issue/1559-2d-entry-below-stock`, no PR yet) edits `generate.rs` beside the `top_stock::note` call and `operation/mod.rs` beside its export; this PR adds one line at each place. Not stacked: based on `upstream/main` (98f093fba). Whichever merges second takes a small merge of main.\n\nChangelog: A rapid at the clearance plane is now judged against the stock: a clearance height set inside the stock is convicted by name and holds the post; MCP add/edit answer with a warning.\nEffort: max (issue labelled effort:high; not escalated)\n\nFixes #2121\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX\n",
